From: "library-check[bot]" <library-check@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 06:13:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(globalize-guide): state the Vite 8 host floor for
 @vitejs/plugin-react-swc

@vitejs/plugin-react-swc only added vite@^8 to its peer range in 4.3.0;
4.0.0-4.2.3 peer ^4 || ^5 || ^6 || ^7. The five SWC setup references state
>= 4.2.3 as the host floor, which cannot install on a Vite 8 project:

  npm error peer vite@"^4 || ^5 || ^6 || ^7" from @vitejs/plugin-react-swc@4.2.3

4.2.3 is the swc_core ABI floor (its @swc/core@^1.15.11), not an installable
floor. On Vite 8 the installable floor is 4.3.0. This matters most on the
population these references are written for: a project reaching the SWC
variant because it has @vitejs/plugin-react@6, which declares a required
peer of vite@^8.0.0 and is therefore always on Vite 8.
